  "question": {
    "text": "The length of the diameter of the circle which touches the $x$-axis at the point $(1,0)$ and passes through the point $(2,3)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TKE5p",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{10}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "4bzek",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3}{5}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "djbOh",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{6}{5}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Pk8qv",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{5}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $(h, k)$ be centre.\n$\\begin{array}{ll}\n(h-1)^2+(k-0)^2=k^2 & \\Rightarrow h=1 \\\\\n(h-2)^2+(k-3)^2=k^2 & \\Rightarrow k=\\frac{5}{3}\n\\end{array}$\n$\\therefore$ diameter is $2 \\mathrm{k}=\\frac{10}{3}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/YRrSooJmvtNjsCdHLejVWr9hDvhYVbsSQaKbe2VhSwQ.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
